Project Description: Smart Hybrid Search for Mobility Improvement Measures

Within the Mobility Division, various functional areas define and manage a wide range of improvement measures aimed at 
enhancing operational efficiency, sustainability, and innovation. These measures are made accessible to users through a 
centralized web-based application, where stakeholders can browse, review, and analyze initiatives across departments.

This project focuses on enhancing the search capabilities of the application by introducing a smart hybrid search solution. 
The goal is to significantly improve how users discover relevant measures by combining traditional keyword-based search 
with advanced semantic search techniques.

The hybrid search functionality enables two primary modes of interaction:

Keyword Search: Users can directly retrieve specific measures using exact identifiers such as measureId, ensuring fast and precise lookup.
Semantic Search: Leveraging vector embeddings, users can search using natural language queries. The system identifies and returns 
measures that are semantically similar or contextually related to the search input, even if exact keywords are not present.

To support this capability, the project implements a comprehensive data pipeline that ensures data is continuously processed and 
indexed for optimal search performance. The pipeline includes the following stages:

Data Extraction: Collecting improvement measures from various source systems across functional areas.
Data Transformation: Cleaning, structuring, and enriching the data, including the generation of vector embeddings that capture semantic 
                     meaning.
Data Loading: Preparing and storing the processed data in a format suitable for search indexing.
Search Index Update: Uploading both the structured data and corresponding embeddings into Azure Cognitive Search, 
                     enabling hybrid querying across textual and vector-based representations.

By integrating semantic intelligence into the search experience, this project empowers users to discover relevant measures more 
intuitively, reduces dependency on exact terminology, and enhances overall usability of the application.

Ultimately, the solution contributes to improved knowledge accessibility and supports better decision-making across the Mobility Division.